From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:56:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/27] prime: canary evidence from canary checks (SOV-P-002
 W8)

An own canary registered with POST /sovereignty/canary (now a token-only
route for the lazarus-canary sidecar, not demo-gated) schedules one extra
request_full_block of that gateway's newest job, sovereignty-canary-check-secs
(45) later, at most one per sovereignty-canary-check-gap-secs (300) per
gateway. The reply counts only if its transactions hash to the job's merkle
branches (verify::job_txids), so a gateway cannot answer with a list its
miners are not hashing.

The detector reads own/shared/decoy hits from these checks
(entropy::features_checked): a canary is judged by jobs first seen
12-180 s after delivery. Job snapshots keep the timing and cluster
features only. POST /sovereignty/check is the demo ingest for harnesses
without a DATUM session.

Ported to origin/main f14bb4c for publication: the check rides on the
found-block transaction request only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
